The provided code is using the `Assert` class from the `System` namespace to make assertions about the state of the `ArrayList` object. The assertions are checking the last index of `x` in the new array list, which should be less than or equal to the size of the old array list. This ensures that the list maintains its size when performing certain operations, such as `Add` and `Remove`.--------------------```cs
Debug.Assert(Old_arrListCount >= 0); // Old array list count should be greater than or equal to 0
Debug.Assert(New_arrListCount >= 0); // New array list count should be greater than or equal to 0

Debug.Assert(Old_arrListIndexOfX == -1 || Old_arrListIndexOfX < Old_arrListCount); // Old index of x in old array list should be the same as old array list count or be less than it
Debug.Assert(New_arrListIndexOfX == -1 || New_arrListIndexOfX < New_arrListCount); // New index of x in new array list should be the same as new array list count or be less than it

Debug.Assert(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX == -1 || Old_arrListLastIndexOfX < Old_arrListCount); // Old last index of x in old array list should be the same as old array list count or be less than it
Debug.Assert(New_arrListLastIndexOfX == -1 || New_arrListLastIndexOfX < New_arrListCount); // New last index of x in new array list should be the same as new array list count or be less than it

Debug.Assert(New_arrListContainsX == Old_arrListContainsX); // New array list should contain x if and only if old array list contains x
Debug.Assert(New_arrListIndexOfX == -1 || New_arrListIndexOfX == Old_arrListIndexOfX); // New index of x in new array list should be the same as old index of x in old array list
Debug.Assert(New_arrListLastIndexOfX == -1 || New_arrListLastIndexOfX == Old_arrListLastIndexOfX); // New last index of x in new array list should be the same as old last index of x in old array list

Debug.Assert(New_arrListCount == Old_arrListCount + 1); // New array list count should be one more than old array list count
Debug.Assert(New_arrListIndexOfX == Old_arrListIndexOfX); // New index of x in new array list should be the same as old index of x in old array list
Debug.Assert(New_arrListLastIndexOfX == Old_arrListLastIndexOfX); // New last index of x in new array list should be the same as old last index of x in old array list

Debug.Assert(New_Ret >= 0); // New ret should be greater than or equal to 0

Debug.Assert(New_arrListContainsX == Old_arrListContainsX); // New array list should contain x if and only if old array list contains x
